* Post-quantum cryptography on blockchains
** What breaks
*** Account signatures (ECDSA, EdDSA)
*** Validator signatures (BLS, Ed25519)
*** Pairing-based proofs
*** Hashes and proof-of-work survive
*** Long vs short exposure
** Migration patterns
*** 1. New post-quantum account or output
*** 2. ZK proof of seed knowledge
*** 3. Sunset legacy signatures
** Bitcoin
*** BIP-360 P2MR (draft)
*** BIP-361 legacy sunset (draft)
*** SHRINCS hash-based signature
** Ethereum
*** EF post-quantum team (2026)
*** leanSig hash-based consensus
*** EIP-8051 ML-DSA, EIP-8052 Falcon
left side
** Other chains
*** Solana: Falcon, Winternitz vault
*** Cardano: research framework
*** Aptos: AIP-137 SLH-DSA
*** Sui: ZK seed proof
*** XRP Ledger: ML-DSA on AlphaNet
*** Algorand: Falcon state proofs live
** Privacy and permissioned
*** Zama: TFHE lattice, pairing proof not PQ
*** Aztec: roadmap to 2030
*** Canton: no published plan
** Post-quantum native
*** QRL: XMSS since 2018, ML-DSA-87 in 2.0
*** Quantus: ML-DSA mainnet 2026
